window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Portlock’s secrets are about to explode. Implode? Some kind of ‘plode anyway.</b></p> <p>After the shit that went down in Chrome Mine, I’m beginning to fear that I may never see <i>my</i> Sidnee again, because the Sidnee I’ve been left with? She’s downright scary.</p> <p>Just as we try to catch our breath, calamity strikes anew: the Mayor’s son has been murdered, and suspicion is being thrown around like confetti—from the mayor himself to nearly half the town, including the usually mild-mannered Sidnee.</p> <p>To make matters worse, several young vampire girls have vanished. Blame is rampant and furious factions are tearing the town apart, making our cosy home anything but.</p> <p>As if all that were not enough to contend with–which it certainly was!–Connor’s father, the Vampire King of America, is on his way to uncover exactly what is going on in our little supernat town. It is suddenly very apparent that I am not quite ready to meet the in-laws, especially when Connor is so clearly freaking the heck out.</p> <p>My own happily ever after has never seemed so far away.</p> <p><b><i>Dive into this fast-paced urban fantasy series if you love mystery, humour, found family, and a slow-burn romance.</i></b></p> <p><b>Don't miss the rest of the Portlock Adventures!</b></p> <p>The Vampire and the Case of her Dastardly Death, a prequel.</p> <p>The Vampire and the Case of the Wayward Werewolf, Book 1.</p> <p>The Vampire and the Case of the Secretive Siren, Book 2.</p> <p>The Vampire and the Case of the Baleful Banshee, Book 3.</p> <p>The Vampire and the Case of the Cursed Canine, Book 4.</p> <p>The Vampire and the Case of the Perilous Poltergiest, Book 5.</p> <p>The Vampire and the Case of the Cozy Christmas, Book 5.5.</p> <p>The Vampire and the Case of the Hellacious Hag, Book 6.</p> <p>The Vampire and the Case of the Malevolent Mermaid, Book 7</p>"; 
